.<|>10)\n##\n(\"relationship\"<|>DYNAMIC RECRYSTALLIZATION<|>STATIC RESTORATION<|>Structures developed by dynamic restoration are thermodynamically unstable and are modified by static restoration when held at temperature.<|>8)\n##\n(\"relationship\"<|>STATIC RESTORATION<|>STATIC RECOVERY<|>Static recovery is one of the static-restoration processes that can operate after hot working.<|>9)\n##\n(\"relationship\"<|>STATIC RESTORATION<|>STATIC RECRYSTALLIZATION<|>Static recrystallization is identified as one of the static-restoration processes that can operate after hot working.<|>8)\n##\n(\"relationship\"<|>SOFTENING MECHANISMS<|>DYNAMIC RECRYSTALLIZATION<|>Dynamic recrystallization is described in relation to the three softening mechanisms associated with hot working.<|>7)\n<|COMPLETE|>"}, "metrics": {"attempted_request_count": 1, "successful_response_count": 0, "failed_response_count": 0, "responses_with_tokens": 1, "prompt_tokens": 2688, "completion_tokens": 3877, "total_tokens": 6565, "compute_duration_seconds": 31.28386616706848, "streaming_responses": 0, "retries": 0, "requests_with_retries": 0}}}